   SESSION designators     the free 100 block on board P (U101, U102, Q101 to Q106, D101, D102, RT101, R101 to R117, C101 to C106, TP101 to TP106); RT1 on board A, which carries no RT designator
   SESSION net names       BRK_VIN (Q2's source, the breaker's input), BRK_SNS, BRK_GATE, BRK_TMR, BRK_PWR, BRK_UVLO, BRK_G2, BRK_H, BRK_HD, BRK_PGD, BRK_CMID, INH_NTC, INH_REF, INH_OUT, INH_G; DOCK_EN_OUT and DOCK_EN_RET on all three boards
   SESSION J_SMB pins      a JST-XH 1x7 at both ends: 1 to 4 unchanged, 5 DOCK_EN_RET, 6 the return (the ground between), 7 DOCK_EN_OUT at the row's end
   SESSION dock positions  J_DOCK and J_BLK pins 3 (DOCK_EN_RET) and 5 (DOCK_EN_OUT), pin 4 ground between them; pin 5's neighbours 4, 6 and 11 are all ground
   SESSION input bypass    C104 and C105, 2.2 uF 50 V X7R in series (1.1 uF) at the sense pair: TI SNVS452G section 10 ('a 1-uF ceramic capacitor to ground close to the drain of the hot swap MOSFET') and 11.1.1; in series as C11 and C12 are (board P's O-12)
   SESSION comparator      U102, TI OPA187IDBVR, a zero-drift amplifier on BRK_VIN used as the comparator: 4.5 to 36 V, its input range from 0.1 V under its negative rail, its offset over temperature read from the held sheet (section 3); C106 its bypass
   SESSION reference       R111 147 kOhm over R112 1.62 kOhm (1653.06 ohm against the trip's 1653), R113 15 MOhm of hysteresis, all from BRK_VIN as the NTC's bridge is (ratiometric)
   SESSION PGD gating      U101's PGD on BRK_PGD at half BRK_VIN (R116, R117 1 MOhm); Q106 holds Q105's gate low while PGD is high; Q105 pulls UVLO; R114 and R115 halve U102's output for Q105's gate
   SESSION test points     TP101 BRK_VIN, TP102 BRK_UVLO, TP103 DOCK_EN_OUT, TP104 DOCK_EN_RET (E-12); TP105 INH_NTC, TP106 INH_OUT (E-12b)
   SESSION lands           the VSSOP-10, SMC, SOD-123, SOT-23-5 and 2512 lands the kit already uses; the 7-circuit XH header of the same row; RT1 on board P's 0402; RT101's 10 mm leads on the project's LeadLands_1x02
   SESSION DD-5 ideal diode round 4: Q109 CSD17570Q5B beside Q1 (source SCP_OUT, drain SW) under U105 LM74700QDBVRQ1 (ANODE SCP_OUT, CATHODE SW, GND the cells' negative); C111 220 nF 50 V on VCAP; R130 10 MOhm gate to source; EN from BRK_VIN through D104 1N4148W with R131 1 MOhm to ground; C112 and C113 100 nF in series at the anode, C114 and C115 470 nF in series at the cathode; TP109 on the gate (E-12d); a second FET beside Q1, not a second driver on Q1's gate
   SESSION B-R2 detector   round 3, route R1: U103 and U104 (OPA187, U102's part), U103 on R10's cell side through R120 200 ohm and C109 470 nF against R118 1.15 MOhm over R119 200 ohm from REV_VZ (BRK_VIN through R129 47 kOhm under D103, the BZT52C12 board A's D25 uses); U104 on PACK_P over R121 332 kOhm and R122 33.2 kOhm against BRK_SNS over R123 328 kOhm and R124 33.2 kOhm (0.05 %, 10 ppm/K), C110 1 nF; Q107 and Q108 2N7002 in series on DOCK_EN_RET, their gates at half of each output (R125 to R128); C107, C108; TP107, TP108 (E-12c)

3. C-1c'S BUDGET (DD-8): the window from l9stk 15.4b, the NTC from Murata's sheet, the comparator from TI's held OPA187 sheet (SBOS807E)
   the window: allow from 77.25 C, block from 83.20 C, trip 80.22 C +-2.97 K with the NTC at 1653 ohm; the NTC's +-1.02 K and +-1.95 K left: consistent
   the NTC (Murata NXRT15XH103FA1B010): R25 10000 ohm, B25/85 3434 K printed as a reference value, 0.12 mA at most, 1.5 mW/K, 10 mm leads;
     its tolerance at 80 C (the record's +-1.02 K) is ASSUMED from the product search sheet: to be confirmed by Murata's approval sheet or E-15
   the bridge at the trip: R110 150 kOhm over the NTC, 0.1155 V at the pack's least 10.6 V, 3.143 mV/K there (B/T^2 0.02750 per K); 0.111 mA at 16.8 V
   the reference: R111 147 kOhm over R112 1.62 kOhm with R113 15 MOhm at the output low: 1652.88 ohm against 1653 (+0.003 K); hysteresis 0.359 K nominal, 0.363 K at most
   the comparator, U102 OPA187 (read, high-voltage table): VOS 10 uV, drift 0.015 uV/K to 125 C, IB 7.5 nA and IOS 14.5 nA over temperature, PSRR 1 uV/V;
     supply 4.5 to 36 V (absolute 40 V) against BRK_VIN's 29.2 V clamp; input range from 0.1 V under its negative rail; at most 54.1 uV in all: 0.017 K
   the bridge and reference resistors: 0.1 % and at most 25 ppm/K between 25 and 101.0 C, each at 0.290 %, the worst of all signs: 0.317 K
   the NTC's own heating at 0.111 mA: 0.014 K (it reads hot)
   THE SPLIT OF +-1.95 K: allow side 0.710 K used (comparator, resistors, own heating, hysteresis, nominal), 1.240 K left for the pad-to-NTC gradient;
     block side 0.336 K used, 1.614 K left; the checker's split asked about 0.9 K for the gradient, the comparator at most 0.47 K, the hysteresis at most 0.5 K: the split closes
   THE LOCKOUT AT THE ALLOW EDGE: a unit tripping at 77.25 C needs its pad within 1.00 K of the 76.25 C inside air before it restarts; at that air the cells' hot stop has already shut the kit down
   E-10 gains: VDS under 1.62 V during current-limit excursions (PGD stays high, so the inhibit stays gated)

3b. B-R2, THE CHARGE THROUGH A LATCHED BREAKER (route R1, round 3): task L4-E11 19h and 15c (round 9's; copied at ecb598c5), the makers' sheets
   the open case (L4-E11 19h): a latch while a source holds VSYS keeps CELL+ tied to it, 10.4 V into the 0.915 ohm fault, so the
     inhibit (CELL+ under 1.98 V) sets only for faults under 33 mOhm; the latched FET at 1.2567 A (R-b's largest) is held at 142.2 C, 1.405 A is its
     safe level (150 C held from 76.25 C at VSD 1 V and 52.5 C/W); a charge over it rested on the firmware
   NO EXISTING ELEMENT TELLS BOARD A (read from the sheets and the drafts):
     PGD switches on VDS alone (SNVS452G pin 8: active when VDS decreases below 1.25 V); a reverse charge makes VDS negative, so PGD reads good
     the -1 has no fault pin: its latch holds GATE low on the 1.75 to 2.6 mA sink until UVLO or VIN cycles (8.4.3); its GATE to OUT clamp is an
       internal 12 V zener (8.4.2), and a divider on GATE draws from the 10 to 22 uA charge pump that sets l9stk's 40.7 ms start (IF-1)
     the enable loop's two conductors: board A reads DOCK_EN_OUT and DOCK_EN_RET only, both ratiometric to BRK_VIN through RT1; their ratio is
       RT1     5 kOhm: RET/OUT 0.8148 with R106 in the loop and 0.8148 with R106 bypassed (a change of the loop's source scales both alike)
       RT1    47 kOhm: RET/OUT 0.3188 with R106 in the loop and 0.3188 with R106 bypassed (a change of the loop's source scales both alike)
       RT1   338 kOhm: RET/OUT 0.0611 with R106 in the loop and 0.0611 with R106 bypassed (a change of the loop's source scales both alike)
       a changed return resistor is confounded with RT1's own 5 kOhm to 338 kOhm span, a raised return enables the breaker undocked (Q103 on
       with no dock), and only the return held LOW is distinct: Q103 then reads the loop open, Q104 pulls UVLO, the -1 resets
     C-1c's NTC reads the pad, too slow and gated by PGD (high in reverse); the gauge's charge FET Q1 could block a charge, but the owner's
       criterion takes Q1 and Q2 welded
   ROUTE R1 SELECTED: board P detects the charge itself and holds the loop's return low, which J_DOCK pin 3 already carries to board A;
     a reset is harmless exactly then: a charge flows backwards only while the source holds CELL+ above the cells, and board A's inhibit holds
     the battery FETs off through the restart, so the dv/dt start meets CELL_FUSED alone and no forward current
   U103, THE CHARGE INTO THE CELLS on R10 (2 mOhm, read from gen_sch_p.py): 0.08694 A per volt of REV_VZ; REV_VZ is BRK_VIN x 0.96074 under
     D103 (BZT52C12: 11.4 to 12.7 V at 5 mA, 6.0 to 10.0 mV/K, under 0.1 uA at 8.0 V; 13.46 V at most at the held 101.0 C case)
     REV_VZ at least 7.95 V wherever BRK_VIN puts it over that (the zener's knee under 1 mA is not printed: its leakage at 8.0 V, ten times hot, through R129)
     tolerances: R118 and R119 0.58 % together, R129's share 0.080 %, R10 1.57 % (its 1 % and 75 ppm/K ASSUMED, owed to Layer 6), U103 33.0 uV
       (VOS, drift to 125 C, IOS through 200 ohm each side, PSRR over 10.6 to 29.2 V)
     BRK_VIN  4.70 V: the threshold 0.368 to 0.418 A
     BRK_VIN  7.60 V: the threshold 0.605 to 0.666 A
     BRK_VIN 10.60 V: the threshold 0.661 to 0.922 A
     BRK_VIN 13.70 V: the threshold 0.661 to 1.187 A
